# XSH getpgid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getpgid.001
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       In the caller's session, with child c1 leading its own group and
           child c2 a member of it, getpgid(c1) and getpgid(c2) both return
           c1, and getpgid() of the caller's own ID returns getpgrp().
test       t/001-other-process.c

assertion  XSH.getpgid.002
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       getpgid(0) in c2 (a member, not the leader, of c1's group)
           returns c1.
test       t/002-zero.c

assertion  XSH.getpgid.003
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#ERRORS/ESRCH
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       getpgid() of the ID of a child whose status has been collected
           (and which no process has reused) returns (pid_t)-1 with ESRCH.
test       t/003-esrch.c

assertion  XSH.getpgid.004
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#ERRORS/EPERM
class      required
since      2008
says       getpgid() of a child that started a session of its own (so its
           group is its ID) returns that ID or fails with EPERM.
note       Whether a process in another session may be asked is left to
           the implementation.
test       t/004-other-session.c

assertion  XSH.getpgid.005
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#ERRORS/ESRCH
anchor     functions/getpgid.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      required
since      2008
says       getpgid(-1) returns (pid_t)-1 with ESRCH (no process has that
           ID) or EINVAL (the may-fail error for an invalid pid).
test       t/005-negative.c
